{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Of Chanoch, the family of the Chanochi.</b> Rashi, of blessed memory, explained: because the nations would disparage them and say, 'On what basis do these trace their lineage to their tribes, to their fathers' houses?' — thinking that the Egyptians had not had their way with their wives — therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, placed His name upon them: a ה at the beginning and a י at the end (i.e., the letter-pattern of יה), to say: I testify concerning them that they are the children of their fathers. And this is what was expressed through David, of blessed memory (Psalms 122:4): ששם עלו שבטים שבטי י״ה עדות לישראל — 'whither the tribes go up, the tribes of YHWH, as a testimony unto Israel' — this name testifies concerning them to their tribes. Therefore in all of them it is written החנוכי, הפלואי, הכרמי, החצרוני, but in Yimnah there was no need to write הימני, because the name is fixed in it with a י at the beginning and a ה at the end (ימנה)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:12.775757790Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}